In plain words: you may read the source code. You may run the editor and use it for anything,
including commercial work. Everything you make with the editor is yours to use, ship and sell.
You may not copy, modify or redistribute the source code or the editor itself.
The legal text follows; where it differs from this summary, the text decides.

1. WHAT THIS COVERS

"C-Bricks" means the files in this repository (the editor's GDScript source, the runtime C files in
scripts/runtime/, the icons, the examples, the documentation, the tools and the tests), and the
editor built from them. "The Editor" means a built, ready-to-run copy of C-Bricks released by the
author. It does NOT include the Third-Party Components of section 6, which keep their own licenses.

2. THE SOURCE CODE

The source code of C-Bricks is made available to read. Except as section 4 allows for Output, you
may not copy, modify, adapt, translate, sublicense, sell, publish or distribute the source code or
any part of it, you may not build another program, editor, code generator or service from it, and
you may not use it to train a model or to build a competing product. Cloning or forking the
repository on GitHub, and viewing it there, is allowed as far as GitHub's Terms of Service give
that right to everyone; that is the only copying this license permits.

3. THE EDITOR

You may download the Editor from the author and run it, free of charge, for any purpose, personal or
commercial. You may not redistribute, resell, sublicense, modify or reverse engineer the Editor
(except where the law gives you that right regardless of this license), and you may not offer it as
a hosted service. To let someone else have the Editor, point them to where the author publishes it.

4. WHAT YOU MAKE WITH THE EDITOR ("OUTPUT")

"Output" means everything the Editor creates or helps you create: your projects (the .cbricks,
.cbscene and project.cbproj files and your assets), the C source and headers it generates, the
exported project folders (Makefile, CMakeLists.txt, build scripts, README), the programs built from
them for any platform, and the .exe / .html / binaries you build. It includes the C-Bricks runtime
files (the contents of scripts/runtime/ and the generated cbricks.h and cbricks_*.c) as they appear
inside your Output.

The author owns no part of your projects. The author grants you a worldwide, perpetual, irrevocable,
royalty-free license to use, copy, modify, publish, distribute, sublicense and sell Output,
including the runtime files embedded in it, for any purpose, commercial or not, under any license
you choose, with no attribution required (credit is appreciated, not required). The runtime
files are licensed this way only as part of Output: you may not pull them out to redistribute them
on their own or to build a competing tool (section 2 applies to them then).

The examples: when you open an example, the Editor makes a copy for you; that copy is Output.
Parts of Output that come from Third-Party Components (section 6) stay under those components'
licenses; NOTICE.md says which ones can end up in your programs and what each asks of you.

5. NO WARRANTY, NO LIABILITY

C-BRICKS, THE EDITOR AND THE OUTPUT'S RUNTIME FILES ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
NON-INFRINGEMENT. THE AUTHOR IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THEIR
USE, INCLUDING DATA LOSS OR PROBLEMS IN PROGRAMS YOU BUILD AND SHIP.

6. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Some files are not the author's and are under their own licenses, which this license does not
change: everything in thirdparty/ (raylib and what it contains, Watt-32, CWSDPMI, the Crynwr packet
driver, DMXOPL), the Godot Engine inside the Editor, and the programs the Toolchains window
downloads (zig, DJGPP, DOSBox-X, Emscripten, CMake). NOTICE.md lists them with their licenses and
where their source is.

7. ENDING

If you break section 2 or 3, the permissions of those sections end for you. The grant in section 4 for
Output you already made stays, because it is given for Output, not for the Editor.

8. GENERAL

If a part of this license is unenforceable, the rest stays. This license is not legal advice and the
author is not offering one.
